\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Field-validated mean absolute error (MAE, plants per 3$\times $3 m quadrat) of count models against the 2026 ground-truth plots. Models are scored within each elevation phase and split by prediction regime: \textit {interpolation} (plots inside the sampled range) versus \textit {extrapolation} (the Antero site, 86 km beyond it; low elevation only). \textit {n} columns score all plots (zeros included), \textit {occ.} columns occupied plots only; `---` marks the gp()-based Bayesian models, whose spatial term extrapolates unreliably beyond the sampled range, so out-of-domain errors are not reported.}}{29}{table.1}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Observed plant counts per 3$\times $3 m quadrat on occupied plots (count $>$ 0) in each area, giving the scale against which the mean absolute errors in the preceding table should be read.}}{30}{table.2}%
